{
  "case_id": "2012-12-142",
  "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJAY P. LEFKOWITZ, ESQ., New York, New York; on behalf of Petitioner.\nANTHONY A. YANG, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Petitioner.\nDAVID C. FREDERICK, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jay P. Lefkowitz",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a classic case of impossibility preemption. Federal law required generic sulindac to have the same ingredients, the same warning and the same safety profile as the branded version. But a New Hampshire jury imposed liability because sulindac didn't have a different safety profile, meaning a different ingredient or a different warning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Lefkowitz, could I understand something just about the scope of your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So tell me, is -- is it now your position, and it seems to be, that any time the FDA approves a product that there can never be a tort liability claim because the FDA's approval is now the ceiling of what you can do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anthony A. Yang",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "New Hampshire law applies a hybrid design-defect standard that imposes liability for harm caused by a product if the product, in light of the manufacturer's warnings, is unreasonably dangerous. Now, that standard falls within the traditional way that this Court has looked at impossibility preemption in Mensing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. YANG",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Let me draw a distinction if --\nthat I think might help.\nWhen the Federal government were to say --\nlet's go -- stay with avocados -- that avocados must\nhave at least 7 percent oil. And the State says, you\nknow what, we think it actually needs 8 percent oil.\nIt's not impossible to comply there. But what we have\nhere is a comprehensive regulatory scheme, where an\nexpert agency with the relevant information makes an\nexpert judgment based on sound -- sound scientific\nevidence that this drug is, in fact, safe and effective"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DAVID C. FREDERICK\nON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what the Solicitor General seeks to argue here is evidence that was not in the record and in which Mutual's own expert who created this evidence testified in deposition he didn't give it to the FDA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the SG says that the FDA did have this right, did have it and did consider it, and that's incorrect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you want me to write down in this case, from my understanding, that under New Hampshire law, strict liability is determined quite without reference to the adequacy of warning?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the warning relevant or not relevant to the determination of strict liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but then if you apply this -- what is deeply bothering me in all these cases, and it's why I came up and said, the FDA has to tell us -- you know."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just -- just to -- because my memory is failing me, is this drug still on the market?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This argument about stopping the sale of the drug completely seems to me to eliminate the impossibility -- impossibility preemption, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "road. That would seem to me to be a very clear impossibility case, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is your point in this case that obstacle preemption has been waived?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no such thing then as a brand name manufacturer can change some design features of the drug -- you know, without FDA approval or without going back to square one of the FDA, there's nothing like that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you respond to the argument, Mutual's argument that they have -- in 2005, they made -- this drug produced $7 million."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is rather incredible to hear counsel talk about how the warnings were not the issue in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It says on page 5496, adequacy of the warning, I guess, the judge says, is not an issue before this jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e3f70a1d435bdea9ca82f1074ab50b188f3766d7f10b8c30547ddc5b83ec78f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e3f70a1d435-0002-0016",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-12-142",
